[38;2;124;124;124mThe disintegration theorem says: Given a probability measure μ on a standard [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mBorel space X and a Borel map f: X → Y to a standard Borel space Y, there exists[0m[38;2;124;124;124ma kernel K: Y → Δ(X) such that:[0m
